<row>
  <col>
    <h2>Alignment inside a column</h2>

    <p>
      By default this deck centers the two columns vertically (<c>columns</c> in <c>deck.json</c>). Here the code is pinned to the
      top of its column with <c>valign=start</c> on the <c><code></c>; a slide can do the same for everything with <c>valign: start</c>.
    </p>
  </col>
  <code lang=rust id=g1 valign=start>
    <frame>
      fn main() {
          let name = "slides";
          println!("hello, {name}");
      }
    </frame>
    <frame>
      fn main() {
          let name = "slides";
          let count = 3;
          for i in 0..count {
              println!("{i}: hello, {name}");
          }
      }
    </frame>
  </code>
</row>
